<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Festus Forward | The Reality</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #f8fafc;
            --text: #1e293b;
            --corporate-blue: #004a99;
            --reality-red: #991b1b;
            --accent: #f8fafc;
        }

        body { font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); margin: 0; padding-top: 60px; }
        #main-nav { background: #fff; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 15px; text-align: center; position: fixed; top: 0; width: 100%; z-index: 1000; }
        #main-nav a { margin: 0 10px; color: #333; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; }
        
        .hero { background: #000; color: white; padding: 80px 20px; text-align: center; }
        .hero h1 { font-size: 3rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        
        .container { max-width: 800px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 20px; }
        
        /* The Accordion/Card Style */
        details { background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 15px; padding: 15px; cursor: pointer; }
        summary { font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
        summary::after { content: '+'; font-size: 1.5rem; }
        details[open] summary::after { content: '-'; }
        
        /* The Spin vs Reality Layout */
        .spin-box { background: #f1f5f9; padding: 15px; border-left: 4px solid var(--corporate-blue); margin: 15px 0; }
        .reality-box { background: #fef2f2; padding: 15px; border-left: 4px solid var(--reality-red); margin: 15px 0; }
        .label { font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 5px; display: block; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <nav id="main-nav"></nav>

    <header class="hero">
        <h1>Festus Forward</h1>
        <p>A "community information" site (that really just wants you to stop asking questions).</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        
        <h2>Project Overview</h2>

        <details>
            <summary>What is the size of the project?</summary>
            <div class="spin-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--corporate-blue)">Corporate Spin</span>
                "We listened to you! We downsized from 12 buildings to just 4."
            </div>
            <div class="reality-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--reality-red)">Reality Check</span>
                The 4-building plan was the original baseline design. They floated a massive 12-building "worst-case" scenario so they could look like the good guys when they "compromised" on the plan they actually intended to build all along.
            </div>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>How will this impact local water?</summary>
            <div class="spin-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--corporate-blue)">Corporate Spin</span>
                "It's a closed-loop cooling system. We reuse water and produce almost zero discharge."
            </div>
            <div class="reality-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--reality-red)">Reality Check</span>
                Internal engineering reports (Horner & Shifrin) prove the local water authority is already maxed out. They are hiding confidential figures because if you knew the real capacity numbers, you’d know there’s no water left for the project.
            </div>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Are there any plans for on-site power plants?</summary>
            <div class="spin-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--corporate-blue)">Corporate Spin</span>
                "No power plant. Just clean utility power from Ameren and backup generators for testing."
            </div>
            <div class="reality-box">
                <span class="label" style="color:var(--reality-red)">Reality Check</span>
                "Backup generators" is a euphemism for a massive array of diesel-burning engines that will roar during grid stress. They haven't disclosed the environmental impact of the air permits they'll need for these "backups."
            </div>
        </details>

    </div>

    <script>
        fetch('nav.html')
            .then(response => response.text())
            .then(data => { document.getElementById('main-nav').innerHTML = data; });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
